Package: strtools
Title: String Cleaning and Tools for Exploratory Data Analysis
Version: 1.0.0000
Authors@R: 
    person("Alvis", "Lee", , "alee134@u.rochester.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: This package includes three functions for working with messy text-based data. 
    str_clean() harmonizes noisy string data by matching values to a user-supplied dictionary. 
    str_find() locates and returns rows containing user-supplied keywords. 
    str_unique() summarizes categorical string values by returning counts and proportions of unique entries. 
    These functions are designed to support exploratory data analysis and preprocessing workflows. 
    It is recommended to use str_clean() first before the other functions for the best results.
    Included in this package are three custom dataframes and 2 dictionaries to illustrate varied use cases across different data structures.
    Refer to R/data.R and data-raw/datasets.R for more information on the datasets.
